ifa/issues/055 -- FA does not converge (final_pass=51, pass_limit_hit=1, 58 violations) on plcfrs's splitgrammar() shape, reduced to 9 lines. Needs all four of: a tuple unpack in the generator feeding a set, a set difference, enumerate(), and two dicts over the same pairs with SWAPPED key/value. This is NOT the shared-CreationSet defect fixed by PYC_CSSPLIT -- that one is fixed and its own repro passes. CPython prints 2, which the check file records, so this flips to PASS when the remaining plcfrs non-convergence is fixed.
